{
  "$comment": "What rpg-ai needs from a world backend (the in-house wiki and VTT, or a Foundry-backed one: the operator, 2026-11-24, \"Have an option to directly integrate with Foundry VTT via actors and journals instead of using our in house vtt and wiki\"). Every ability rpg-ai calls, by extension, with its arguments, what it answers and the fields rpg-ai reads; `required` ones a backend must offer for play, the rest it may leave out (rpg-ai then does without). An ability with `called_by` is one rpg-ai doesn't call itself but its play depends on another caller reaching (the routing between backends). Held by server/extensions/ai_chat/Backends_test.py: each loaded_ability rpg-ai calls is listed here, everything listed without `called_by` is called, and the in-house backends offer every required one.",
